{"id":"line-slope","title":"Slope through two points","problemType":"line-slope","skill":"slope","skillTitle":"Slope","grade":"8","strand":"algebra","standards":[{"standardId":"8.EE.B.5","facet":"Find and interpret slope from points tables and graphs","basis":"editorial"},{"standardId":"8.EE.B.6","facet":"Find and interpret slope from points tables and graphs","basis":"editorial"}],"script":{"id":"line-slope","title":"Slope through two points","seed":"film","shots":[{"figure":{"view":[-1,-1.5,9,10.5],"points":{"A":[3,2],"B":[5,8],"C":[5,2]},"parts":[{"id":"ax","start":true,"axes":true,"step":1,"every":2},{"id":"line","seg":["A","B"],"ink":"accent","w":6,"extend":[4.2,4.2]},{"id":"run","seg":["A","C"],"ink":"blue","w":7},{"id":"rise","seg":["C","B"],"ink":"warm","w":7},{"id":"dA","dot":"A","ink":"gold","r":13},{"id":"dB","dot":"B","ink":"gold","r":13},{"id":"lA","label":"(3,2)","at":"A","dir":"w"},{"id":"lB","label":"(5,8)","at":"B","dir":"e"},{"id":"lA2","label":"(3,8)","at":"A","dir":"w"},{"id":"lB2","label":"(5,2)","at":"B","dir":"e"},{"id":"lrun","label":"2","at":"run","dir":"n","ink":"blue","size":"l"},{"id":"lrise","label":"6","at":"rise","dir":"e","ink":"warm","size":"l"},{"id":"lrise2","label":"-6","at":"rise","dir":"e","ink":"warm","size":"l"}]},"beats":[{"say":"Slope measures how steep a line is.","do":[{"do":"draw","target":"line","at":"Slope","dur":1.2}]},{"say":"Take two points on it: three, two, and five, eight.","do":[{"do":"show","target":["dA","lA"],"at":"three"},{"do":"show","target":["dB","lB"],"at":"five"}]},{"say":"From the first to the second, x changes by five minus three, which is two.","do":[{"do":"draw","target":"run","at":"x"},{"do":"write","tex":"\\text{change in }x=5-3=\\cb{2}","fresh":true,"id":"i1","at":"changes"},{"do":"show","target":"lrun","at":"two"}]},{"say":"And y changes by eight minus two, which is six.","do":[{"do":"draw","target":"rise","at":"y"},{"do":"write","tex":"\\text{change in }y=8-2=\\cw{6}","fresh":true,"id":"i2","at":"changes"},{"do":"show","target":"lrise","at":"six"}]},{"say":"Slope, written m, is the change in y over the change in x: rise over run. Six over two is three.","do":[{"do":"term","word":"slope","meaning":"How steep a line is: rise over run, the change in $y$ divided by the change in $x$ between two of its points. Written $m$.","at":"Slope"},{"do":"highlight","target":"lrise","at":"rise"},{"do":"highlight","target":"lrun","at":"run"},{"do":"write","tex":"m=\\dfrac{\\cw{6}}{\\cb{2}}=3","fresh":true,"id":"i3","at":"Six"}]},{"say":"For each step to the right, this line climbs three.","do":[{"do":"highlight","target":"line","at":"climbs"}]},{"say":"Now tilt the line so it falls. Going right, y drops from eight to two.","do":[{"do":"hide","target":["lA","lB","lrise"],"at":"tilt"},{"do":"move","points":{"A":[3,8],"B":[5,2],"C":[5,8]},"at":"tilt","dur":1.5},{"do":"show","target":["lA2","lB2"],"at":"drops"},{"do":"write","tex":"\\text{change in }y=2-8=\\cw{-6}","fresh":true,"id":"i4","at":"drops"},{"do":"show","target":"lrise2","at":"two"}]},{"say":"The change in y is negative six, so the slope is negative three. A line that falls has a negative slope.","pause":0.4,"do":[{"do":"highlight","target":"lrise2","at":"negative"},{"do":"write","tex":"m=\\dfrac{\\cw{-6}}{\\cb{2}}=-3","fresh":true,"id":"i5","at":"slope"},{"do":"highlight","target":"line","at":"falls"}]}]},{"figure":{"view":[-7,-6.5,6,2.5],"points":{"P1":[-4,-4],"P2":[3,-2],"C":[3,-4],"RL":[-2,-4]},"parts":[{"id":"ax","start":true,"axes":true,"step":1,"every":2},{"id":"line","seg":["P1","P2"],"ink":"accent","w":6,"extend":[4,4]},{"id":"run","seg":["P1","C"],"ink":"blue","w":7},{"id":"rise","seg":["C","P2"],"ink":"warm","w":7},{"id":"d1","dot":"P1","ink":"gold","r":13},{"id":"d2","dot":"P2","ink":"gold","r":13},{"id":"l1","label":"(-4,-4)","at":"P1","dir":"nw"},{"id":"l2","label":"(3,-2)","at":"P2","dir":"nw"},{"id":"lrun","label":"7","at":"RL","dir":"s","ink":"blue","size":"l"},{"id":"lrise","label":"2","at":"rise",